+# ColossusX frontend modifications
+
+Date: 2026-09-21. Based on Blockscout frontend v2.7.2, commit
+`446c409eeb54274aab90ff371a705f9699cd84ef`. Code modifications are GPLv3;
+the original project license and third-party notices are retained.
+
+- Apply the ColossusX network name, mascot assets, metadata, chart watermark,
+  donation address and CypherTroopers GitHub link.
+- Enlarge desktop navigation mascots to 40/42 px and fit the collapsed sidebar,
+  preserving the 30/32 px mobile layout. Use a close-up mascot favicon bundle.
+- Retain Blockscout attribution and original wordmark in the footer; include
+  copyright, legal notices, corresponding source and displayed build version.
+- Disable advertisements and account/wallet transaction integrations. Remove
+  optional Dynamic, Reown, Specify and Multisender SDK dependencies and imports.
+  Vendor the MIT wagmi 2.19.5 hook package without its connector entry point or
+  connector dependency; keep its upstream license and a dated change notice.
+- Preserve read-only contract information and manual signature verification.
+- Prefer backend API counts, including zero, over delayed statistics counters.
+  Refresh homepage counters and visible data every 30 seconds.
+- Derive daily transactions and the chart from the same UTC series; handle day
+  rollover, focus and visibility refresh and unavailable values explicitly.
+- Display FHS-D block production, common miner PoW and common RPC rewards from
+  the backend's verified wei amounts, with linked payout recipients and exact
+  category breakdowns. Preserve pending versus verified zero and avoid applying
+  Ethereum transaction-fee arithmetic to native FHS-D rewards. Refresh pending
+  block rewards every 30 seconds until indexing completes (2026-09-21).
+- Keep the v2.7.2 hot-contract ranking, filters, event timestamps, search contract
+  markers and supported token presentation. Chain-dependent data still requires
+  indexing and relevant transactions/contracts on the connected network.
+- Limit Next.js build workers for the deployment host; pin the Node build image,
+  provide the complete Docker build stages and embed the source archive SHA-256
+  into the resulting image's metadata.
+
+Source archive generation adds the build entry point, fonts and CC0 license
+texts, and deployed mascot files. Dependency lockfiles and build instructions
+are included. Runtime secrets, caches and installed dependencies are excluded.
